            <title>[LU-21344] TCU: Timestamped trash entries in a striped dir's .Trash cannot be looked up: name hashes to another stripe than its stub</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21344</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;For a DNE striped directory, &lt;tt&gt;&amp;lt;dir&amp;gt;/.Trash&lt;/tt&gt; is a virtual directory whose stripes are the per-MDT Trash Can stubs of the directory's shards. With &lt;tt&gt;trash_can_delete_policy=timestamp&lt;/tt&gt;, a repeated deletion of the same name is stored as &lt;tt&gt;&amp;lt;name&amp;gt;.&amp;lt;timestamp&amp;gt;&lt;/tt&gt;: &lt;tt&gt;mdd_trash_insert_obj()&lt;/tt&gt; keeps the stub chosen for the original name and inserts the timestamped name into that same stub.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A lookup through the virtual &lt;tt&gt;.Trash&lt;/tt&gt; hashes the full timestamped name in &lt;tt&gt;lmv_locate_tgt_by_name()&lt;/tt&gt;, so it can go to another stripe than the stub that holds the entry. Then:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;readdir of &lt;tt&gt;.Trash&lt;/tt&gt; lists the entry, but &lt;tt&gt;stat&lt;/tt&gt;/lookup of it fails: with ENOENT if the stripe it hashes to has a stub, with ENODEV if that stripe has no stub;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;rm -f &amp;lt;dir&amp;gt;/.Trash/&amp;lt;name&amp;gt;.&amp;lt;timestamp&amp;gt;&lt;/tt&gt; returns 0 but leaves the entry;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;other operations by path through &lt;tt&gt;.Trash&lt;/tt&gt; (e.g. restore) are likely affected the same way (not tested).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
